host Ubuntu cloud pier — Eastern (EDT) time convention
title ALES98 — Lotus's top-and-tail trimmer, the third reading of ALES95's segmentation
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; after ALES97 sent, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, self-approve, prove GREEN, send as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think ALES96 removes EVERY silent run and closes ranks; ALES97 cuts AT every silence and keeps each region apart. Between those two sits the single most-used silence gesture of all — TOP AND TAIL: trim only the dead air at the start and the end, keep every pause inside. Lindy-first that is a century-old reflex on every tape machine; crux-first it is the third honest reading of one segmentation — ALES96 read it to remove all silence, ALES97 to split on all silence, ALES98 to bound the content — the first Lotus rung whose result is the original clip narrowed to its living span, internal pauses intact.
think Correctness is composition against BOTH neighbours. The span law: the trimmed clip equals the original over [first_nonsilent.start, last_nonsilent.end) byte for byte, hand-built by an independent segment scan. The bracket law ties it to ALES97 and ALES96 at once — it equals the original bracketed by the split's outer takes byte for byte (the coalesce preserves the outer non-silent boundaries), and trim_silence.len <= top_and_tail.len <= original.len, equal to the full trim only when there is no interior gap. So the rung is cross-checked against the two tools that read the same segmentation to different ends.
think The one real edit care: cut the TAIL first, then the head. A suffix cut shifts nothing before it, so the leading run's start index stays valid for the second cut. Held that order with an invariant on each cut span. Degenerate paths named plainly: all-silent -> no non-silent run found -> cut the whole clip to empty; no-silent -> lead_count and tail_count both zero -> unchanged.
obs First witness run GREEN on the first pass — span-law grid (8 frame lengths x 4 floors x 3 splits), bracket-law grid against ALES96 and ALES97, the interior-pause-kept case (strictly longer than the full trim on a gapped clip), all-silent->empty, no-silent->unchanged, only-leading and only-trailing, and four named refusals. TAME style bans clean; width-check clean on the new module.
obs No custody gate reached — software only, local; no funds, keys, network, device, or real speaker. It edits only by removing whole classified-silent frames at the two ends through ALES2's cut, never a sample between the first and last non-silent runs.
loom witness=ales_top_tail_witness green=1 laws=7 span_law_grid=96 bracket_law_grid=20 module_bytes=15k
file lotus/top_tail.rye ALES98 — top_and_tail() finding the first and last non-silent runs and cutting only the leading and trailing silence through ALES2's cut, tail first.
file tools/ales_top_tail_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs the selftest, asserts the GREEN line.
file active-designing/20260814-234106_fill-ales98-lotus-top-tail-trimmer.md the self-approved design read naming the span law, the bracket law, and tail-first cut order.
file lotus/README.md front door — the ALES98 rung and status roster synced.
recommend keep-going — the next Lotus crux builds on this living-span result (a leader/trailer pad that keeps a chosen margin of silence at each end, a normalize-across-takes pass, or a min-take-length filter that drops too-short regions), each its own self-approved round; no custody gate reached.
